<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,465.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,465.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,465 today from 1,454 on March 12, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1488    13.513	  1488    13.513</p>
<p>   1a   1462 11075.000	  1461 11063.000</p>
<p>   2    1778    25.406	  1752    25.031</p>
<p>   2a   1803 14788.000	  1792 14694.000</p>
<p>   3    1662    15.331	  1646    15.188</p>
<p>   3a   1537 12131.000	  1505 11881.000</p>
